(go/type Edge "Edge represents a CFG edge.\nExample edges for b branching to either c or d.\n(c and d have other predecessors.)\n\n\tb.Succs = [{c,3}, {d,1}]\n\tc.Preds = [?, ?, ?, {b,0}]\n\td.Preds = [?, {b,1}, ?]\n\nThese indexes allow us to edit the CFG in constant time.\nIn addition, it informs phi ops in degenerate cases like:\n\n\tb:\n\t   if k then c else c\n\tc:\n\t   v = Phi(x, y)\n\nThen the indexes tell you whether x is chosen from\nthe if or else branch from b.\n\n\tb.Succs = [{c,0},{c,1}]\n\tc.Preds = [{b,0},{b,1}]\n\nmeans x is chosen if k is true.\n" (struct

    ^{:line 102 :tag (* Block) :doc "block edge goes to (in a Succs list) or from (in a Preds list)\n"} b




    ^{:line 107 :tag int :doc "index of reverse edge.  Invariant:\n  e := x.Succs[idx]\n  e.b.Preds[e.i] = Edge{x,idx}\nand similarly for predecessors.\n"} i))


