^{:go/breaks [[7 398]] :go/end 399} (go/method LackingPos "LackingPos indicates whether b is a block whose position should be inherited\nfrom its successors.  This is true if all the values within it have unreliable positions\nand if it is \"plain\", meaning that there is no control flow that is also very likely\nto correspond to a well-understood source position.\n" ^bool [^{:tag (* Block)} b]
  ;; Non-plain predecessors are If or Defer, which both (1) have two successors,
  ;; which might have different line numbers and (2) correspond to statements
  ;; in the source code that have positions, so this case ought not occur anyway.
  (when (!= (.-Kind b) BlockPlain)
    (return false))

  (when (!= (.-Pos b) src/NoXPos)
    (return false))

  (range [_ v (.-Values b)]
    (when (.LackingPos v)
      (continue))

    (return false))

  true)


